<title>Tools, data, and formulas</title>

<subsection> 
 <title>Tools</title>
<p>The standalone tools below are the previously introduced simulation zyTools for one proportion 
(<url href="https://learn.zybooks.com/zybook/GRACEMAT2000JohnsonFall2023/a9ead249-be3a-1cea-2e87-7bb963727c38" rel="noopener noreferrer">
2.12</url>) and one mean (<url href="https://learn.zybooks.com/zybook/GRACEMAT2000JohnsonFall2023/bc553747-b533-fd11-aeca-e2816608da2d" rel="noopener noreferrer">
3.10</url>) with expanded capabilities for computing confidence intervals. Additionally, a tool 
for simulating theory-based confidence intervals from population parameters is included as well. </p>

 
